    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get the theory about \"service quality,\" but that feels like a luxury for a cafe that's struggling just to keep the lights on. It feels like the \"nuance\" usually ends up favoring the politicians making these rules rather than the actual business owners living with the consequences. Is there any real evidence that this actually helps the local economy in the long run, or is it mostly just a way to force small, local shops out so big corporations can take over the market?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
