      "content": "Many studies actually contradict the \"corporate takeover\" fear, showing that in smaller towns, wage hikes often strengthen the local economy by keeping money within the community and allowing small, family-owned businesses to survive, which can actually reduce the \"corporate consolidation\" you're trying to avoid. While there is no magic bullet for tight margins, evidence suggests that the cost of stocking up on a stable, happy workforce is frequently more financially viable for a single small shop than the alternative of constant staff turnover and empty chairs.",
